ithub-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMzMzMTIzOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865#issuecomment-333331238"},"message":"Would be nice to have a full log with timestamps enabled to see what's going on and what exactly the time  is spend on. I doubt it's the dry run of add. (BTW I think we don't call anything \"to be compatible\" with direct mode, but __in__ direct mode only)\nOr enable a line profiling for `add`. Or may be we can even have a reproducible scenario? ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1506800600,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMzMzMTQ0MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865#issuecomment-333331441"},"message":"Somebody needs to write a test that generates a few thousand files and saves them. All slowness is long before any git call.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1506801129,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMzMzMTk3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865#issuecomment-333331972"},"message":"Here is the test:\n\n```sh\ndatalad create\nfor i in $(seq 10000); do echo $i \u003e $i.txt; done\ndatalad add .\n```\n\nEverything, including the staging of the added files takes few seconds, and then the big sleep...\n\nThis would run for 5min on my system. git-annex does it in a few seconds.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1506803115,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMzMzMzc4Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865#issuecomment-333333782"},"message":"Thanks. I think I got it and it's us! ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1506807456,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMzMzNzU5OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865#issuecomment-333337598"},"message":"@bpoldrack was spot on: the culprit is the use of `swallow_logs` in `Dataset.repo`. With it removed the runtime for the above code is down from 5min to:\n\n```\ndatalad add .  20,09s user 5,31s system 109% cpu 23,270 total\n```\n\nFor comparison (on the same problem with 10k files)\n\n```\nbash -c \"git annex add .; git commit -m save\"  9,94s user 4,40s system 90% cpu 15,844 total\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1506807663,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMzMzNzc5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865#issuecomment-333337792"},"message":"also, for this particular `add` call there was not a single undesired log message after removing the `swallow_log` call.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1506809297,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMzMzOTEzNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865#issuecomment-333339135"},"message":"what!? swallow logs had such a detrimental effect???\nhow come -- was it raising loglevel or smth?  just interested to know\nand yeah -- ideally code should not have any of those swallows now I guess.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1506838942,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMzM1NjYwNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865#issuecomment-333356606"},"message":"\u003e how come -- was it raising loglevel or smth? just interested to know\n\nNot sure, what you mean by this. The call of `swallow_logs()` has no paramters. It did not involve a new level.\n\nAnd just FTR: confirming Michael's experience with the little test above.\nCurrent implementation:\n`datalad add .  255.72s user 7.60s system 100% cpu 4:21.94 total`\nRemoved `swallow_logs()`:\n`datalad add .  25.92s user 6.16s system 108% cpu 29.506 total`","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1506869024,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMzM4MTQwMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865#issuecomment-333381402"},"message":"Great\nRe new level: \n`def swallow_logs(new_level=None, ...`","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1506869304,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMzM4MTY4OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865#issuecomment-333381688"},"message":"Okay, so the answer is: No. There was no new log level, that caused this issue.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507049051,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMzkwNjA0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865#issuecomment-333906048"},"message":"Update: not sure how it was possible, but I merged master now, and removed `swallow_logs` from `Dataset.repo` manually, then ran `add` on the manyfiles dataset again:\n```\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 36402)\n  save (ok: 1)\ndatalad add .  239,26s user 32,19s system 118% cpu 3:49,39 total\n```\n\nThis time includes all annexing and everything. Not fast, but not ultra-slow either. I am surprised how it not crash due to the nargs issue seen above. Maybe we have something clever in place. This time the dataset wasn't mixed-dirty, but only had things untracked that were actually added... Anyways, DATALAD!\n\nAlso, metadata aggregation in its current form is slow as f* but actually holds up to 36k files -- this is with all bells and whistles (annex and DICOM files-based metadata...):\n\n```\n[INFO   ] Update aggregate metadata in dataset at: /tmp/study_20140724_095117357 \naggregate_metadata(ok): /tmp/study_20140724_095117357 (dataset)                                                       \n[INFO   ] Attempting to save 4 files/datasets \nsave(ok): /tmp/study_20140724_095117357 (dataset)\naction summary:\n  aggregate_metadata (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\nDATALAD_RUNTIME_RAISEONERROR=1 datalad --dbg aggregate-metadata  925,79s user 7,32s system 96% cpu 16:06,51 total\n```\n\nand now after some personal touch:\n\n```\nDATALAD_RUNTIME_RAISEONERROR=1 datalad aggregate-metadata  302,41s user 2,26s system 99% cpu 5:05,09 total\n```\n\nabout ~3min of which is plain pydicom reading the header of the DICOMs. Good enough....","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1507421331,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTI4MzAyODk3OA=="},"status":2},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1541430617,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzNTkwOTMyMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865#issuecomment-435909320"},"message":"Just came back top this issue to see where we are in this respect with -revolution:\n\n```\nmih@meiner /tmp/alot % . ~/env/datalad3-dev/bin/activate\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/alot % datalad rev-create\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/alot \ncreate(ok): /tmp/alot (dataset)                                                                                              \n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/alot (git)-[master] % for i in $(seq 10000); do echo $i \u003e $i.txt; done\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/alot (git)-[master] % datalad rev-save\n....\nadd(ok): 9999.txt (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 10000)\n  save (ok: 1)\ndatalad rev-save  23.04s user 8.76s system 129% cpu 24.613 total\n```\n\nfor comparison with the same test scenario:\n\n```\n% time bash -c 'git annex add . \u003e /dev/null; git commit -m \"test\" \u003e /dev/null'\nbash -c 'git annex add . \u003e /dev/null; git commit -m \"test\" \u003e /dev/null'  8.60s user 6.27s system 104% cpu 14.198 total\n```\n\nTen sec more (without any parallelization), which is quite a bit faster than the original 3:49min. Importantly the save stage is now almost instantaneous, and pretty much all time is spent on add.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1541433916,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzNTkzMDQ2NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1865#issuecomment-435930465"},"message":"cool","files":null}]}